  "description": "LOSVIA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C52 H86 N12 O58 Tb9 1+,7(C1 H4 O1),N1 O3 1-. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3A (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb4A (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb5A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.566-5.258 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.10-169.30°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C59H114Tb9N13O68. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
